	</header>

	<section id="search">
	  <div class="wrap">
	    <div class="sec-head">
	      <div class="eyebrow">// search</div>
	      <h2>Finds the note you meant</h2>
	      <p>Full-text, fuzzy, and tag-aware out of the box. Watch it rank as the query builds.</p>
	    </div>

	    <div class="demo">
	      <div class="demo-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>vault — smart search</span></div>
	      <div class="demo-body">
	        <div class="demo-tree" id="tree"></div>
	        <div class="demo-main">
	          <div class="search-box">
	            <span style="color:var(--text-3)">⌕</span>
	            <span id="typed"></span><span class="cursor"></span>
	          </div>
	          <div class="search-hint">tab toggles semantic · #tag and /folder filter · ⌥↵ asks the agent</div>
	          <div class="results" id="results"></div>
	        </div>
	      </div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section id="privacy" style="background:var(--bg-2); border-block:1px solid var(--border);">
	  <div class="wrap privacy-wrap">
	    <div>
	      <div class="eyebrow">// privacy</div>
	      <h2 style="text-align:left">Your notes stay yours</h2>
	      <p style="color:var(--text-2); font-size:16.5px; margin:12px 0 22px;">
	        Run a local model and nothing ever leaves your machine. Use a cloud one and you decide, per note, what it may see.
	      </p>
	      <div class="toggle-row">
	        <button class="tg on" data-mode="local">Local model</button>
	        <button class="tg" data-mode="cloud">Cloud provider</button>
	      </div>
	      <ul class="privacy-list">
	        <li><span class="ck">✓</span><span><strong>Untrusted by default.</strong> Cloud providers start blocked from every private note.</span></li>
	        <li><span class="ck">✓</span><span><strong>Private-by-default vaults.</strong> Only notes you allow can be read, embedded, or sent.</span></li>
	        <li><span class="ck">✓</span><span><strong>Staged edits.</strong> Nothing is written to disk until you approve the diff.</span></li>
	      </ul>
	    </div>

	    <div class="flow">
	      <div class="machine">
	        <span class="machine-label">your machine</span>
	        <div class="node-row">
	          <div class="fnode"><strong>vault</strong><span>1,284 notes</span></div>
	          <span class="arrow">→</span>
	          <div class="fnode"><strong>plugin</strong><span>index + agent</span></div>
	          <span class="arrow" id="arr2">→</span>
	          <div class="fnode" id="localModel"><strong>ollama</strong><span>local model</span></div>
	        </div>
	      </div>
	      <div class="cloud-zone">
	        <div class="barrier blocked" id="barrier">✕ nothing crosses this line</div>
	        <div class="cloud-node" id="cloudNode" style="opacity:.4">☁ cloud provider — idle</div>
	      </div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section id="agent">
	  <div class="wrap">
	    <div class="sec-head">
	      <div class="eyebrow">// agent</div>
	      <h2>It reads before it answers</h2>
	      <p>Searches your vault, opens what's relevant, and stages every edit for review.</p>
	    </div>
	    <div class="agent">
	      <div class="agent-head"><span style="color:var(--accent)">●</span> chat — project notes</div>
	      <div class="agent-body" id="agentBody"></div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section style="background:var(--bg-2); border-block:1px solid var(--border);">
	  <div class="wrap">
	    <div class="sec-head">
	      <div class="eyebrow">// everything else</div>
	      <h2>Built for daily use</h2>
	    </div>
	    <div class="fgrid">
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">memory</span><h4>It remembers you</h4><p>Opt in and the agent keeps its own notes on your preferences and projects — as real notes in your vault, yours to read and edit.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">skills</span><h4>Teach it your tools</h4><p>Bundled skills for exploring your vault, editing notes and searching the web. Write your own as plain notes.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">mcp</span><h4>Connect anything</h4><p>Attach MCP servers to give the agent any external tool or data source.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">.chat</span><h4>Branching history</h4><p>Chats are files in your vault. Editing a message forks a branch instead of erasing the old one.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">vision</span><h4>Images and PDFs</h4><p>Send them to models that support it — capability is detected per model, not assumed.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">subagents</span><h4>Delegate</h4><p>Hand focused work to another agent with its own model, tools and clean context.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">parallel</span><h4>Many chats at once</h4><p>Run several conversations simultaneously — none blocks another.</p></div>
	      <div class="fcell"><span class="k">pointers</span><h4>Never goes stale</h4><p>Memory stores links to where facts live in your vault, not copies — so answers reflect your current notes.</p></div>
	    </div>
	  </div>
	</section>

